    "text": "Two groups are said to be isospectral if they have the same set of element\norders. Suppose that G is a finite group such that every finite group isospectral to G\nis isomorphic to G. Is it true that the quotient of G by its socle is solvable?\n                                                                                     D. O. Revin",
